---
description: PascalCase filenames for React components; camelCase for non-component helpers
globs: 'components/**/*.ts,components/**/*.tsx,lib/**/*.tsx'
alwaysApply: true
---

# React component filenames

Match the filename to what the file primarily exports:

| Export | Filename | Example |
|--------|----------|---------|
| React component (default or named) | **PascalCase** `.tsx` | `BrandMarkIcon.tsx`, `LandingPageHeaderActions.tsx` |
| Non-component helper, hook, or util | **camelCase** `.ts` / `.tsx` | `useUploadState.ts`, `formatPrice.ts` |

## Examples

```
components/LandingPage/
  LandingPageInner.tsx          # exports LandingPageInner component
  LandingPageHeaderActions.tsx  # exports LandingPageHeaderActions component
  landingPageTestCommon.ts      # test fixture helpers only (if added)
```

## Exceptions

- Next.js app router files keep framework names: `page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`,
  `icon.tsx`, `route.ts`
- `*.stories.tsx`, `*.test.tsx`, `*.module.css` follow their own conventions
- `index.ts` barrel files

ESLint does not enforce this split (helpers and components both live under
`components/`), so follow this rule when adding or renaming files.
